igned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we get the following projection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{8} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ Equivalently, it is the acute angle between $x$ and any non-zero vector that is parallel to ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ So, to make calculations easier, we can find the angle between the vectors\n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\,{\\text{proj}}_{S}x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{x\\cdot {\\text{proj}}_{S}x}{‖x‖‖{\\text{proj}}_{S}x‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 1+(-5)\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{54}\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{9\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{2}})≈{19.47}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle." 13194139536026 true] [17592186379882 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379883 13194139536026 true] [17592186379882 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379884 13194139536026 true] [17592186379882 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379885 13194139536026 true] [17592186379882 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379886 13194139536026 true] [17592186379882 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379887 13194139536026 true] [17592186379882 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536026 true] [17592186379882 1041 "selection" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379882 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379885 13194139536026 true] [17592186379882 1110 #uuid "1ecade9a-1a07-5690-8fec-47498e02a4d0" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379883 1034 "{21.83}^{∘}" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379883 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536026 true] [17592186379883 1111 #uuid "7615ff4d-be18-5825-a4af-8890e53486d4" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379884 1034 "{17.36}^{∘}" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379884 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536026 true] [17592186379884 1111 #uuid "ec87d9cc-2606-5e2f-829b-33d5e965b2a9" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379885 1034 "{19.47}^{∘}" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379885 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536026 true] [17592186379885 1111 #uuid "2cdea0aa-4fa4-5aa4-89bc-fd49fcce9bf4" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379886 1034 "{20.02}^{∘}" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379886 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536026 true] [17592186379886 1111 #uuid "b3e054ba-4c25-55ff-a17b-d79ad1e72654" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379887 1034 "{18.88}^{∘}" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379887 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536026 true] [17592186379887 1111 #uuid "a45b6b6b-61c0-585b-90f8-2d170537f7dc" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379888 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379889 13194139536026 true] [17592186379888 1089 "q-83649" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379888 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536026 true] [17592186379888 1100 "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 6{x}_{1}-12{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379888 1113 #uuid "c652198c-eb51-5ff9-a8db-886e24ee0c6e" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379888 1145 "First, we need to find a basis for the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 0 & -12 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}$ are free variables. Now, from the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{3}.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is the basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nNow, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379889 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379890 13194139536026 true] [17592186379889 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379891 13194139536026 true] [17592186379889 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379892 13194139536026 true] [17592186379889 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379893 13194139536026 true] [17592186379889 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379894 13194139536026 true] [17592186379889 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536026 true] [17592186379889 1041 "selection" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379889 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379892 13194139536026 true] [17592186379889 1110 #uuid "ac217634-801a-567a-9f93-a201df830e92" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379890 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379890 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536026 true] [17592186379890 1111 #uuid "c5ebdc4c-e88e-5ddd-af6b-4e5e9ac7f665" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379891 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379891 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536026 true] [17592186379891 1111 #uuid "180ea0a8-4891-59c2-9fda-d5e72708d991" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379892 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379892 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536026 true] [17592186379892 1111 #uuid "9901b6e4-675f-5432-b5af-43fcac5ebc61" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379893 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536026 true] [17592186379893 